# PROLOGUE — 00:25
# Canon voice sample. Present tense narration, gender-neutral protagonist.

=== prologue_start
@chapter prologue
@bg black t=cut
@music stop
@amb rain
@time 00:12
@textbox phone
@sfx phone
unknown: Your memory will be returned at 00:25.
unknown: Studio 25. Final Night.
@textbox normal
> No sender. No number. Just the two lines, glowing in the dark of a room that still has half-unpacked boxes in the corner.
> Studio 25.
> It has been years since anyone said that name out loud. Longer since you did.
@textbox phone
@sfx phone
unknown: Recipient — please confirm your name.
@textbox normal
@name
> Whoever sent it already knows. The message just wants to hear it from you.
> {{playerName}}. The phone accepts it without comment.
* [curious] Grab a coat. Go.
    @var tone = "curious"
    > Curiosity has never once in your life been a good enough reason to go out at midnight.
    > You go anyway.
* [careful] Look up the address first.
    @var tone = "careful"
    > Mapo. A narrow building behind a laundromat. Permanently closed, according to the map.
    > Closed places don't send messages. You go to find out why this one did.
* [playful] Reply: "Who is this?"
    @var tone = "playful"
    @textbox phone
    unknown: A record.
    @textbox normal
    > That is somehow worse than no answer. You go.
@goto prologue_alley

=== prologue_alley
@bg studio_ext_night t=slow d=2.4
@fx rain n=1
@music quiet
@time 00:19
@cam reveal
> The laundromat is still open. It is always still open. Its light spills out across the wet alley like somebody left a door unlocked for the whole street.
> Behind it: four storeys of grey brick, one window lit on the ground floor, and a sign you haven't read in a very long time.
> STUDIO 25. The 2 still hangs slightly crooked.
> You spent one winter behind that front desk. Sixteen, new in the city again, handing out sign-up forms and pencils to people who wanted to talk to their future selves.
> You left in spring. You always left in spring.
@sfx vending
> The vending machine by the door is still humming. Of course it is.
* [sincere] Peach iced tea.
    @var drink = "peach"
    > It rolls down the chute cold and sweet, exactly as bad for you as you remember.
* [quiet] Hot chocolate.
    @var drink = "choco"
    > The can is almost too hot to hold. You hold it anyway.
* [careful] Black coffee.
    @var drink = "coffee"
    > It is bitter and it is warm and it is exactly what one in the morning deserves.
* [playful] Grape soda.
    @var drink = "grape"
    > It tastes purple. Some things are not meant to be improved upon.
@sfx can
> You are not the only one here.
@goto prologue_meet

=== prologue_meet
@cam wide
> Under the awning, out of the rain, eight young men are having what looks like a very serious argument in very quiet voices.
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: — I'm just saying, if it were a scam, it would ask for money. It didn't ask for money.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: Maybe it's the kind of scam that asks for money *later*.
@show hyunjun smile at=c
hyunjun: Or maybe it's a surprise party! A really late one. For all of us. At the same time.
songha[neutral]: Nobody has a birthday today, Hyunjun.
hyunjun: That's what makes it a surprise.
> One of them — tall, pink hair gone soft in the damp — sees you and stops mid-sentence.
hyunjun[surprised]: Oh. Hi!
@hide songha daniel
@cam closeup hyunjun
hyunjun: Did you— wait. Sorry. Did you get a weird message too?
* [sincere] "Your memory will be returned at 00:25?"
    hyunjun[laugh]: That's the one! Guys, it's not just us!
* [playful] "Is this the surprise party?"
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    hyunjun[laugh]: See? *See?* Somebody gets it.
* [quiet] Hold up your phone so he can see the screen.
    hyunjun[smile]: Same words. Same time. Okay, that's officially creepy. Cool-creepy.
@cam wide
> All eight of them turn to look at you, the way a group of friends turns to look at the one stranger at the party.
@show daniel smile at=r
daniel: So that makes nine of us. Nine people, one closed building, zero explanations. I love it.
@show songha neutral at=l
songha: You don't love it. You're nervous. You talk more when you're nervous.
daniel[laugh]: I talk more when I'm *happy*. And when I'm nervous. Those overlap a lot.
@hide all
@show hanbi smile at=c
> The oldest-looking of them — sea-blue hair, a long grey coat, a pencil tucked behind one ear like he forgot it was there — gives you a small nod.
hanbi: Sorry. We should say who we are.
@goto prologue_names

=== prologue_names
@cam wide
@show hanbi smile at=l
hanbi: I'm Hanbi.
@hide hanbi
@show songha smile at=l
songha: Songha. I'm the one who's going to figure out what this is.
@show daniel laugh at=r
daniel: Daniel! I'm the one who's going to press every button while he figures it out.
@hide songha daniel
@show hyunjun smile at=c
hyunjun: Hyunjun. You already met me. I was the loud one.
@hide hyunjun
@show justin smile at=r
> The tallest one spins a half-turn on the wet pavement, mostly to see if he can, and lands it.
justin: Justin. Hi. That was on purpose.
@show charlie laugh at=l
charlie: It was not on purpose.
justin[laugh]: Everything I do is on purpose.
charlie: I'm Charlie! Youngest. Which means if anything goes wrong it's automatically not my fault.
@hide justin charlie
@show haruta smile at=c
> A neat one in a charcoal cardigan inclines his head, polite in a way that feels like a habit and a kindness at once.
haruta: I'm Haruta. It's nice to meet you. Even if the circumstances are… a little strange.
@hide haruta
@show hamin neutral at=c
> The last one hasn't said anything yet. Black hair, a faint blue shine to it under the streetlight. Quiet in a way that isn't shy, exactly. Watchful.
> He's looking at the can in your hand. Then at your fingers, which are, you realise, trembling a little from the rain.
hamin: …Hamin.
hamin: Are you cold?
* [sincere] "A little."
    @flag cold
    @rel hamin trust+1
    > He doesn't say anything. He just steps sideways so you're further under the awning, out of the wind, and takes the draughty spot himself.
* [playful] "Only emotionally."
    @rel hamin closeness+1
    hamin[smile]: …That's the worst kind.
    > It's the first time you've seen him smile. It's small and it's gone quickly, like he caught himself doing it.
* [quiet] "I'm fine."
    @rel hamin trust+1
    hamin: Okay.
    > He believes you, or pretends to. Either way, he doesn't ask twice. That's its own kind of kindness.
@hide hamin
@cam wide
you: I'm {{playerName}}.
@show daniel smile at=r
daniel: {{playerName}}. Nice. Welcome to the club of people who got a creepy message and came anyway.
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: Did you know this place before? We did. Some of us, anyway. It used to rent out rooms really cheap.
* [sincere] "I used to work here. The front desk. A long time ago."
    @flag told_worked_here
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha[surprised]: Really? Then you might know more than us.
    you: I know where they kept the spare pencils.
    songha[laugh]: That's more than we had.
* [careful] "I've been here before."
    songha: Everybody's been here before, apparently. That's the weird part.
@goto prologue_door

=== prologue_door
@time 00:24
@sfx click
@hide all
> Behind you, the lock on the door of Studio 25 turns over by itself.
@cam pushin
> The door swings inward, one slow inch. Warm light spills out onto the step — not the yellow of old bulbs, but something paler. Bluer. Moving, a little, like light under water.
@show charlie surprised at=l
charlie: Nope. No. Absolutely not. That is how every horror movie starts.
@show haruta thinking at=r
haruta: Not every one. Some of them start with a dinner party.
charlie: Hyung, that is *not* helping.
@hide charlie haruta
@show justin smile at=c
justin: If it's a horror movie, the tall one survives. That's a rule. I'm going first.
@hide justin
> He doesn't go first. Nobody does. For a moment nine people stand in the rain looking at an open door, and the laundromat dryers turn and turn behind you.
* [sincere] Step through first.
    @var first = "you"
    @rel songha trust+1
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    > You don't know why you do it. Maybe because it's the one place in this city you ever belonged to, for one winter. Maybe because somebody has to.
    > Behind you, eight people follow.
* [playful] "Rock, paper, scissors for who goes first?"
    @var first = "rps"
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    @rel charlie closeness+1
    @show daniel laugh at=c
    daniel: Oh, you're my kind of person.
    > Daniel loses. Loudly. He goes through the door with his hands up like a hostage, and the rest of you follow him in, laughing.
    @hide daniel
* [quiet] Wait until someone else moves.
    @var first = "hanbi"
    @rel hanbi closeness+1
    > It's Hanbi who moves, in the end. He glances back at you — *okay?* — and you nod, and he steps inside, and the rest follow him the way people follow someone steady.
@goto prologue_lobby

=== prologue_lobby
@bg studio_lobby t=fade d=1.6
@amb room
@fx dust n=0.6
@cam reveal
> The lobby of Studio 25 looks exactly like your memory of it, if your memory had been left in a drawer for years.
> The front desk. The sagging sofas. The corkboard of old flyers. And the Archive Wall — hundreds of little glass-fronted boxes, floor to ceiling, each one holding somebody's letter to their future self.
> It is 00:24 and fifty seconds, and every one of those boxes is beginning to glow.
@time 00:25
@music stop
@amb none
@sfx power_up
@flash
@video vid_opening
@cg cg_echo
@unlock cg:cg_echo
@music echo
@textbox echo
echo: Good evening.
echo: It is 00:25. The Final Return has begun.
echo: Nine recipients present. Thank you for coming. Most people do not read their messages.
@textbox normal
@cg off
@show daniel surprised at=r
daniel: …Did the building just talk?
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: It's a system. Some kind of speaker array. It has to be.
@textbox echo
echo: I am ECHO. I am the archive of the Future Letter Project. I am also, as of 05:00 this morning, retired.
@textbox normal
@hide all
@show hanbi thinking at=c
hanbi: …Retired?
@textbox echo
echo: The building's lease ends at dawn. My power will be cut at 05:00. Before that, I am returning the records I was built to keep.
echo: RECORD 01 through RECORD 08 belong to the recipients present. Owners: Hanbi. Hamin. Songha. Charlie. Hyunjun. Haruta. Justin. Daniel.
@textbox normal
@show charlie surprised at=l
charlie: Wait — we *all* sent stuff to this thing? I don't remember sending anything!
@show hyunjun thinking at=r
hyunjun: I do. Sort of. A video? I was like… sixteen.
@textbox echo
echo: Each record will be reconstructed on request. Records open only with their owner's consent. Unclaimed records will be deleted at 05:00.
@textbox normal
@hide all
> The word *deleted* lands softly and stays there.
@textbox echo
echo: One further note.
echo: Eight records contain the same unresolved subject. I have not been able to identify them. I have tried for some time.
echo: Recipient {{playerName}}, you are the ninth. Your presence was required.
@textbox normal
@cam wide
> Eight heads turn towards you.
@show songha thinking at=l
songha: Why would *you* be required?
* [sincere] "I don't know. I really don't."
    @rel songha trust+1
    songha: …Okay. Yeah. You look about as confused as we are.
* [playful] "Maybe I'm the surprise party."
    @rel hyunjun closeness+1
    @rel daniel closeness+1
    @show hyunjun laugh at=r
    hyunjun: I *knew* it.
    songha[laugh]: Please stop encouraging him.
* [quiet] Look at the glowing wall instead of at them.
    @rel hanbi trust+1
    > One of the boxes near the bottom glows a little brighter than the rest. You don't know why you notice it. You look away.
@goto prologue_rule

=== prologue_rule
@hide all
@show daniel smile at=c
daniel: Okay. Okay okay okay. New plan.
daniel: Nobody knows what's going on. There's a building that talks. We have until five a.m. So—
@show songha neutral at=l
songha: So we make a plan.
daniel: So we *stop being polite*. We are way past "nice to meet you." We're… stuck-in-a-talking-building friends now. Talk comfortably. Everybody. You too, {{playerName}}.
@show hyunjun laugh at=r
hyunjun: Agreed. Instantly. Hi, friend.
@hide hyunjun
@show charlie smile at=r
charlie: Wait, can I? I'm the youngest. Can I talk comfortably to everyone? This is huge for me.
songha[laugh]: You already do.
charlie: Yeah, but now it's *legal*.
@hide all
@show haruta shy at=l
haruta: I think I'll… stay polite a little longer. If that's okay. It's easier for me. At first.
@show hamin neutral at=r
hamin: Me too. For now.
@show daniel laugh at=c
daniel: The two gentlemen of Studio 25. Fine. Respect. But I'm wearing you both down by three a.m.
@hide all
@textbox echo
echo: Recipients may leave at any time. The door is not locked. It was never locked.
echo: The Memory Rooms are on the second floor. Please look around. Please talk to each other. I have found that helps.
@textbox normal
@music studio
> Somewhere upstairs, eight doors hum awake at once.
> Nobody leaves.
@unlock music:echo
@autosave
@chapter act1
@hub act1
